@startuml <SLUG>_Requirements
' =====================================================================
' Requirements Diagram — STARTER TEMPLATE  (Phase 03, diagram 7 of 7) — the traceability backbone
' Builds on: ALL REQ-* in the SyRS. Conventions §7 = the 7-relationship contract.
' Replace <PLACEHOLDERS>; delete (example) lines. Split into high-level vs system-level
' diagrams if one becomes unreadable. Type each REQ by its class→subtype map (Model_Coverage_Matrix.md §6).
'
' THE 7 SysML RELATIONSHIPS (all in scope — containment & copy are NOT optional):
'   derive      REQ -> REQ ONLY; direction = derived(lower) -> source(higher); adds constraints from analysis
'   refine      model element (use case/activity/state) -> REQ; clarifies meaning
'   satisfy     block -> REQ; design fulfils REQ (ASSERTION, not proof)
'   verify      test case / I-A-D activity -> REQ; proof (use TC-VER-TBD until Phase 07)
'   copy        copy REQ ⤳ master REQ; read-only mirror of a reused regulatory/contractual REQ
'   containment parent REQ ⬦— child REQs; compound REQ ("shall do A and B") decomposed by nesting
'   trace       any ↔ any; weak general dependency — use SPARINGLY, only when nothing above fits
' =====================================================================
title <Project Name> — Requirements Diagram (TODO)

' ---------- Requirements (stereotype every node; type by class) ----------
class "REQ-F-<nn>\n<functional statement>"   as REQ_F   <<requirement>>
class "REQ-F-<mm>\n<derived child statement>" as REQ_F2 <<requirement>>
class "REQ-P-<nn>\n<performance statement>"   as REQ_P   <<requirement>>
class "REQ-D-<nn>\n<domain/standard statement>" as REQ_D <<requirement>>
class "REQ-D-<nn>-MASTER\n<reused master REQ>" as REQ_D_MASTER <<requirement>>

' ---------- Compound REQ decomposed via containment ----------
class "REQ-F-<kk>\n<compound: shall do A and B>" as REQ_CMP <<requirement>>
class "REQ-F-<kk>.1\n<child A>" as REQ_CMP_A <<requirement>>
class "REQ-F-<kk>.2\n<child B>" as REQ_CMP_B <<requirement>>

' ---------- Model elements & test cases ----------
' (rendered as classes with stereotypes so they live in the same requirements diagram)
class "<UC: refines a REQ>" as UC <<useCase>>
class "<Design Block>" as BLOCK <<block>>
class "TC-VER-TBD\n<verifies a REQ>" as TC <<testCase>>

' =================== THE 7 RELATIONSHIPS ===================

' 1. derive  — REQ -> REQ ONLY, derived(lower) -> source(higher)
REQ_F2 ..> REQ_F : <<derive>>

' 2. refine  — model element clarifies a REQ
UC ..> REQ_F : <<refine>>

' 3. satisfy — block fulfils a REQ (assertion, not proof)
BLOCK ..> REQ_F : <<satisfy>>

' 4. verify  — test case / I-A-D proves a REQ
TC ..> REQ_F : <<verify>>

' 5. copy    — read-only mirror of a reused regulatory/contractual master REQ
REQ_D ..> REQ_D_MASTER : <<copy>>

' 6. containment — compound REQ decomposed into child REQs (namespace nesting)
REQ_CMP +-- REQ_CMP_A : <<containment>>
REQ_CMP +-- REQ_CMP_B : <<containment>>

' 7. trace   — weak general dependency (LAST RESORT only)
REQ_P ..> REQ_F : <<trace>>

note bottom
  TODO: iterate EVERY REQ-* in the SyRS and apply the correct ONE of the 7 relationships.
  No silent omissions — render every gap as a visible TODO note (e.g. "TODO: assign satisfier").
  Mirror satisfy/verify/derive links into Model_Coverage_Matrix.md and run the negative-space checks.
end note

@enduml
